; Shared lowercase font, 26 glyphs: LOWER_A..Z (a..z). Code indexes FONT_LOWER_LOWER_A + (c - 'a'):
; never insert or reorder tiles. Companion of font.tiles (uppercase, digits, punctuation), same metrics,
; so mixed text sits on one baseline. Use with "common_res": ["font", "font_lower"] in game.json.
;
; Design rules (same weight as font.tiles, black on white):
; - Ascenders (b d f h k l, dots of i j) start at row 0 = cap height; t starts at row 1.
; - x-height 5 px on rows 2-6, baseline row 6; row 7 empty except descenders; column 7 always empty.
; - Most letters 6 px wide (cols 0-5), m w 7 px, i l centred in the 6 px cell; 2 px stems, 1 px bars.
; - Descenders (g j p q y) are the ONLY exception to "row 7 empty": bowl/stem on rows 2-5 and a
;   2-row tail on rows 6-7 (1 px below the baseline). Without that drop, p q read as small caps P Q
;   and g as 9. Cost: in text stacked every 8 px a tail can touch a capital or ascender right below
;   it; leave a blank row between lines when the layout allows it.
; - Look-alikes: l has a flag top-left and a tail right (I has bars, 1 a flag and a base);
;   a is open on the left at row 3, e has a middle bar and is open on the right; c is open;
;   n/h differ by the ascender, u is open on top; g and y curl left, q has a straight stem, y is open on top.

@ LOWER_A
